    "text": "Suppose that X is a free non-cyclic group, N is a non-trivial normal subgroup\nof X and T is a proper subgroup of X containing N . Is it true that [T, N ] < [X, N ]\nif N is not maximal in X?                                               V. P. Shaptala",
